r changes. Existing explicit inventory IDs and routes remain authoritative; do not overwrite or remove explicit entries. Preserve ordinary noncolliding IDs. Surface any instance intentionally omitted because of an explicit route conflict rather than presenting it as independently observed. Choose the smallest identity representation; no durable store or new coordinator.\\n\\nProof: deterministic fixtures for agent_test and agent-test at distinct roots show both discoverable instances retained with distinct valid IDs, stable on reordered scans, and no snapshots or workers attributed to the wrong root. Include discovered-versus-explicit collisions and existing explicit inventory preservation tests. Exercise fleet selection for each resolved instance. Correct original draft example: agent_test and agent-beta do not collide; agent_test and agent-test do.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:56.828Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy worktree 1788550542915580458-critic, git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a (running build revision unknown)\\nObserved: discovery.go:16 keys discovered candidates by root path, so DiscoverLocalInstances can return multiple instances whose sanitized IDs collide: sanitizeID (discovery.go:196-210) maps \\\"agent_test\\\" and \\\"agent-beta\\\" style names to the same ID (both \\\"agent-test\\\", underscores and dashes both normalize to \\\"-\\\"). app.go:239-241 then builds discMap keyed by instance ID, so the second colliding instance silently overwrites the first in the map and, at app.go:275-283, is skipped via existingMap — a working Forest checkout simply never appears in the fleet, with no log or error. The same silent-drop applies if a discovered ID matches an explicit inventory ID.\\nRequired: every discoverable, validated instance must either appear in the fleet or its omission must be surfaced; discovery IDs must be unique per instance or collisions must be resolved deterministically and observably.\\nProposed spec direction: make DiscoverLocalInstances deduplicate or disambiguate by ID (e.g. suffix the ID from the root path on collision) before returning, or make syncDiscoveredInstances log/record dropped collisions; add a discovery test with two sibling dirs whose names sanitize to the same ID.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:46:20.447Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:46:20.447Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"Problem: discovery deduplicates roots but generates IDs with sanitizeID; names such as agent_test and agent-test both become agent-test. Reconciliation keys workers/state by ID, so distinct roots can silently collapse or swap targets across scans.\\n\\nOutcome: discovered instances with distinct normalized roots must not silently share an effective identity. Resolve collisions deterministically before worker/state reconciliation, preserving stable route-to-root binding across repeated scans and input order changes. Existing explicit inventory IDs and routes remain authoritative; do not overwrite or remove explicit entries. Preserve ordinary noncolliding IDs. Surface any instance intentionally omitted because of an explicit route conflict rather than presenting it as independently observed. Choose the smallest identity representation; no durable store or new coordinator.\\n\\nProof: deterministic fixtures for agent_test and agent-test at distinct roots show both discoverable instances retained with distinct valid IDs, stable on reordered scans, and no snapshots or workers attributed to the wrong root. Include discovered-versus-explicit collisions and e