{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_01a06df99bc57a93b35d5151420b840f","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"powder take canopy-tester-envelope-schema-validation --agent \"$POWDER_AGENT\" 2>&1; echo \"EXIT:$?\""},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"canopy-tester-envelope-schema-validation\",\"title\":\"CLI envelope schema version mismatch and envelope malformed JSON rejection lack regression cover\",\"spec\":\"Defend the public Collector.Collect protocol boundary without changing forest.cli.v2 policy. Using the existing injectable CommandRunner, return malformed envelopes and assert a command-attributed CLIError rather than an accepted snapshot. Cover unsupported schema, non-object/malformed JSON, trailing JSON, omitted required envelope fields, and null args. Keep the existing command-mismatch and command-failure tests; do not duplicate them. Cases must use otherwise-valid command data so each fails for its intended reason. Prove collection stops at the offending command and valid envelopes still succeed. No source-string assertions, new decoding abstraction, or mock-echo tests. Run focused collector tests and repository checks.\",\"repo\":\"misty-step/canopy\",\"blocked_by\":[],\"lease\":{\"agent\":\"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\"principal\":\"none\",\"until\":\"2026-09-04T23:51:10.542Z\"},\"ask\":null,\"proof\":null,\"abandoned\":false,\"notes\":[{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T19:39:32.824Z\",\"by\":\"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\"text\":\"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: worktree 1788550542912867580-tester (git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a), running PID 704790 build unknown\\nSurface: collector.go:297 (cliCollector.runJSON), collector.go:343 (decodeCLIEnvelope), collector.go:138 (cliCollector.Collect). Behaviors: Canopy relies strictly on the forest.cli.v2 JSON protocol envelope. When a command runner returns an envelope with an invalid or unexpected schema (e.g. \\\"forest.cli.v1\\\"), missing envelope fields (schema, command, args, exit), or trailing JSON data, Collect must reject the envelope with a *CLIError identifying the schema mismatch or envelope error, and terminate collection without accepting invalid data. Failing example: execute collector.Collect where the runner outputs an envelope with Schema: \\\"forest.cli.v1\\\" or with missing schema field or trailing JSON; today collector_test.go only tests command mismatch (TestCLICollectorRejectsEnvelopeCommandMismatch) and exit status failures; zero tests exercise schema mismatch or envelope JSON structural validation. Acceptance: a Builder adds test cases in collector_test.go asserting that Collect returns a *CLIError with the message mentioning invalid schema when the envelope schema is not \\\"forest.cli.v2\\\", and fails when envelope top-level fields are missing or trailing JSON is present. Observed: collector.go:297-300 and collector.go:356-361 check the schema and top-level envelope fields, but grep reveals no test references invalid schema or envelope field parsing errors. Required: unit tests in collector_test.go covering envelope schema mismatch, missing required envelope keys, and trailing JSON in command output. Proposed test-work: add collector tests in collector_test.go verifying that envelopes with incompatible schema versions, missing top-level keys, or trailing JSON are rejected with a CLIError.\"},{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T19:51:10.542Z\",\"by\":\"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\"text\":\"took\"}],\"created_by\":\"none\",\"promoted_by\":\"none\",\"promoted_at\":\"2026-09-04T19:49:05.527Z\",\"promotions\":[{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T19:49:05.527Z\",\"by\":\"none\",\"spec\":\"Defend the public Collector.Collect protocol boundary without changing forest.cli.v2 policy. Using the existing injectable CommandRunner, return malformed envelopes and assert a command-attributed CLIError rather than an accepted snapshot. Cover unsupported schema, non-object/malformed JSON, trailing JSON, omitted requir