tch, missing required envelope keys, and trailing JSON in command output. Proposed test-work: add collector tests in collector_test.go verifying that envelopes with incompatible schema versions, missing top-level keys, or trailing JSON are rejected with a CLIError.\"},{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T19:51:10.542Z\",\"by\":\"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\"text\":\"took\"}],\"created_by\":\"none\",\"promoted_by\":\"none\",\"promoted_at\":\"2026-09-04T19:49:05.527Z\",\"promotions\":[{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T19:49:05.527Z\",\"by\":\"none\",\"spec\":\"Defend the public Collector.Collect protocol boundary without changing forest.cli.v2 policy. Using the existing injectable CommandRunner, return malformed envelopes and assert a command-attributed CLIError rather than an accepted snapshot. Cover unsupported schema, non-object/malformed JSON, trailing JSON, omitted required envelope fields, and null args. Keep the existing command-mismatch and command-failure tests; do not duplicate them. Cases must use otherwise-valid command data so each fails for its intended reason. Prove collection stops at the offending command and valid envelopes still succeed. No source-string assertions, new decoding abstraction, or mock-echo tests. Run focused collector tests and repository checks.\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-04T19:39:28.732Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-04T19:51:10.542Z\",\"derived\":{\"terminal\":false,\"waiting\":false,\"open\":true,\"live\":true,\"takeable\":false}}\nEXIT:0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788551470586},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.encrypted\",\"data\":\"Q-PaDgFJSeHl5OtQ0AvV8cZzPA8896XIJVRyAR_mE0N9wPI9At8NJEqjlh3vswM0U92SfpppqbBMFrP0HGqiH8z2ubTi-tzlqpTWmKMWMWmK2RexMZDRUK8vI00VrWLUZdF7oZJ27rPmvT6hd3IEhZXJJdVN0b68qtkASBlA6yJB517P2gMbDBbj5Ia8ysiQ7V9s56syfn0_mzJfswTQse7a7lW85PFDRwupBmEgz0s1adyvTfvwNgaB9gpZl5ymRLSeWfF4dxEGp4HD_T6IBlL8xCeo95WC-RY61cp1e4nWshGbQEEMGhjDDDUyX0lyBSBq2tzDKJmxtY0fTpV5vz7cifBfqqtI